-# Smart TV Remote 0.6.3
+# Smart TV Remote 0.6.4
 
 Local Wi-Fi remote for:
 
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 
 The Android app and Windows tester use the same local controller and responsive interface. No companion app is installed on the television.
 
-## Fixes in 0.6.3
+## Fixes in 0.6.4
 
 - Fixed oversized inline Netflix and PlayStation logos in the mobile layout.
 - Reworked the Google TV Remote Service v2 startup sequence to wait for the TV configuration, negotiate only supported features, answer the active-feature request, and report a connection only after `remote_start`.
@@ -25,6 +25,12 @@
 - The UI reports `opened` only after confirmation. Otherwise it shows that launch attempts were sent instead of claiming success.
 - Android builds now use a stable test signing key so future 0.6.x test updates can be installed over 0.6.2.
 
+
+- The selected platform is now verified against the TV ports before connecting. If a Thomson / Google TV IP is entered while Samsung is selected, the app automatically switches to Google TV instead of trying Samsung ports 8001/8002.
+- Saved auto-connect also probes both protocol families, preventing a stale Samsung selection from being reused for a Google TV.
+- The connection screen refreshes the effective platform before showing the connection hint.
+- The displayed app version is updated from the runtime state instead of remaining stuck on 0.6.2.
+
 ## Google TV first connection after upgrading
 
 1. Uninstall an older test APK if Android reports a signature conflict.
